D = {
 "Cult of Asmodeus|MTF": "Asmodeus claims every cult of the Nine, and any NPC leading a diabolical cult must acknowledge him. The most worthy leaders gain the Demands of Nessus trait. At the start of each of its turns, the creature picks an ally it can see within 30 feet. That ally loses 10 hit points and the creature regains the same number. If incapacitated, it doesn't choose. The closest ally within 30 feet is picked instead.",
 "Cult of Atropus, the World Born Dead|MTF": "**Gaze of Corruption (Recharge).** The cultist targets one creature it can see within 30 feet. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution save or take 16 (3d10) necrotic damage and be poisoned for 1 minute. The poisoned target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.",
 "Cult of Baalzebul|MTF": "Baalzebul recruits individuals, offering hope to those whose failures drive them to seek redemption. His boon is the Path of Baalzebul trait. As a bonus action on its turn, the creature picks an ally it can see within 30 feet. Until the start of its next turn, the creature has advantage on all ability checks and attack rolls, while the ally has disadvantage on all ability checks, attack rolls and saving throws.",
 "Cult of Belzenlok|PSD": "The Cabal serves Belzenlok with fanatical dementists, priests, Grimnant knights and assassins. Cultists can gain Demonic Vigor (1/day). As a bonus action, or as a reaction at 0 hit points, the creature regains 1 hit point and gains temporary hit points equal to its Constitution modifier plus its maximum Hit Dice. Favored members gain Unholy Tether. When an ally within 30 feet dies, the creature uses a reaction to regain hit points equal to twice the dead creature's Constitution modifier.",
 "Cult of Borem, of the Lake of Boiling Mud|MTF": "**Borem's Embrace (1/Day).** The cultist touches one creature within 5 feet. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Dexterity save or be coated in sticky, steaming mud. While coated, its speed is halved, it can't use reactions, and it takes 10 (3d6) fire damage at the start of each of its turns. The effect lasts 1 minute, until the cultist is incapacitated or dies, or until the target is immersed in water.",
 "Cult of Dispater|MTF": "Dispater trades in secrets for souls and plots to topple governments and orders. Cultists can gain Infernal Insight (short or long rest recharge). As a bonus action, the creature has advantage on all ability checks and attack rolls until the end of the turn. Leaders may gain Vexing Escape (1/day). As a reaction to taking damage, it reduces that damage to 0 and teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it sees.",
 "Cult of Fierna|MTF": "Fierna manipulates those who seek love or fanatic followers. Cultists can gain Infernal Loyalty. The creature has advantage on saves while it sees a creature within 30 feet with Loyalty beyond Death. Leaders gain Loyalty beyond Death (short or long rest recharge). As a reaction when an ally it sees drops to 0 hit points, that ally drops to 1 instead and gains temporary hit points equal to the leader's Charisma score plus half its Hit Dice.",
 "Cult of Geryon|MTF": "Geryon bargains with those seeking brute strength, such as orcs, ogres and trolls, who form fighting companies and bandit gangs. Members can gain Crushing Blow (short or long rest recharge). As a bonus action, the creature adds its Strength modifier (minimum +1) to the damage of its next melee weapon hit within 1 minute. Leaders gain Indomitable Strength (Recharge 5). As a reaction to damage, it rolls a d10 and subtracts it.",
 "Cult of Glasya|MTF": "Glasya patronizes thieves and corrupt nobles, and her gifts can be turned against family. She grants Step into Shadows (short or long rest recharge). As an action, the creature and its gear turn invisible until the end of its next turn. Leaders gain Infernal Ring Leader. As a reaction when hit by an attack, the creature picks an ally it sees within 5 feet, and that ally is hit instead.",
 "Cult of Haask, the Voice of Hargut|MTF": "**Haask's Presence (1/Day).** The cultist becomes a Tiny slug-like being and teleports onto a Humanoid it sees within 30 feet. The target must succeed on a DC 15 Charisma save or be charmed. While charmed, the cultist controls it on its next turn. At that turn's end, the cultist teleports to an unoccupied space within 30 feet and returns to normal. In slug form it can't be targeted directly but takes area effects normally.",
 "Cult of Levistus|MTF": "Levistus offers escape to those desperate to avoid a seemingly certain fate, often drow. Some pledge their souls for an escape later. His boon is the Path of Levistus trait. The creature teleports to a location of Levistus's choice within 1 mile and regains all its hit points. It can use this as an action or when it would die. It works only once.",
 "Cult of Mammon|MTF": "Mammon spreads greed. Cultists can gain Grasping Hands (short or long rest recharge). As a bonus action, the creature makes a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check contested by Wisdom (Insight) of a creature within 15 feet. On a success, an unheld item up to 10 pounds teleports to its hand. Leaders gain Promise of Wealth (short or long rest recharge). As a bonus action, five allies gain advantage on attacks against one creature until its next turn ends.",
 "Cult of Mephistopheles|MTF": "Mephistopheles, a master of arcane arts, recruits students of magic, such as wizard guilds, sage conclaves, storm giants and oni. Cultists can gain Spell Shield. The creature has advantage on saving throws against spells, and a success gives it temporary hit points equal to the spell's level. Leaders can gain Spell Leech. As a bonus action, the creature picks an ally it sees within 30 feet. That ally loses its lowest-level spell slot and the creature gains it.",
 "Cult of Tharizdun, the Chained God|MTF": "**Tharizdun's Spark (Recharge 6).** As a bonus action, the cultist touches a simple, martial or natural weapon. The next creature hit by that weapon must succeed on a DC 15 Wisdom save or have disadvantage on all ability checks. The target repeats the save at the end of each minute, ending the effect on a success.",
 "Cult of the Black Earth|POTA": "This cult worships elemental earth and wants landslides and earthquakes to ruin civilization. Burrowing monsters such as ankhegs and bulettes serve it. Members are patient, stoic and brutal, never surrender, and live underground. Their sign is a triangle made with thumbs and forefingers. The medusa Marlos Urnrayle leads it with the war pick Ironfang, a gift of Ogremoch. He is vain, cruel and jealous. It allies with the Crushing Wave and distrusts Howling Hatred.",
 "Cult of the Crushing Wave|POTA": "This cult worships water and returns the living to the seas by drowning or bloodshed. Aquatic ghouls, merrows and sharks aid it. Its sign crosses the forefingers with overlapping thumbs. Members are patient, opportunistic mercenary skirmishers and strong swimmers. The one-armed sailor Gar Shatterkeel leads it with the trident Drown, a gift of Olhydra. He is sullen and bitter. The cult likes Black Earth and hates Eternal Flame.",
 "Cult of the Eternal Flame|POTA": "This cult worships destructive fire and wants to purify the world into ash. Fire creatures see its members as allies. Their sign is one hand over a thumbs-up fist, and many bear burn scars. Members are impetuous and violent but inventive, enslaving captives to work forges. The tiefling Vanifer leads it with the dagger Tinderstrike, a gift of Imix. She is a manipulator and fiercely ambitious. The cult hates Crushing Wave.",
 "Cult of the Howling Hatred|POTA": "This cult worships wind and storms to punish those who wronged it. It appeals to illusionists, spies and assassins, and winged beasts serve as steeds. Its sign is an inverted triangle formed by a fist with thumbs and little fingers touching. Members prefer stealth, illusion and ambush from high places. The moon elf Aerisi Kalinoth leads it with the spear Windvane, a gift of Yan-C-Bin. She is a spoiled queen with a violent temper. Eternal Flame is its best ally.",
 "Cult of Tyranthraxus, the Flamed One|MTF": "**Radiant Flames (1/Day).** Multihued flame surrounds the cultist for 1 minute, until it is incapacitated or dies, or until it ends the flame with no action. While inflamed, it has telepathy to 30 feet and can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it sees as a bonus action. Each creature starting its turn within 5 feet makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking 16 (3d10) radiant damage on a failure or half on a success.",
 "Cult of Zariel|MTF": "Zariel's cult offers martial training in war-torn lands to refugees, veterans, knightly orders and mercenaries. Cultists can gain Ferocious Surge (short or long rest recharge). When the creature hits with a non-critical attack, it can make the hit a critical hit. Leaders gain Infernal Tactics. After rolling initiative, if not incapacitated, the creature can swap initiative results among itself and up to three allies it sees.",
 "Demonic Boon of Balor|MTF": "A balor can grant the Fiery Soul trait. The creature has resistance to fire damage. When it dies, it explodes, and each creature within 10 feet takes fire damage equal to its number of Hit Dice.",
 "Demonic Boon of Baphomet|MTF": "Followers gain Unerring Tracker, leaders gain Incite the Hunters, and all gain Labyrinthine Recall (perfect memory of paths traveled). Unerring Tracker: as a bonus action, the creature psychically links to one creature it sees. For 1 hour, it can learn that target's distance and direction as a bonus action. Incite the Hunters (short or long rest recharge): as an action, each ally within 30 feet with Unerring Tracker makes a weapon attack as a reaction against its tracked target.",
 "Demonic Boon of Demogorgon|MTF": "Demogorgon's followers are lone killers driven by his whispering voice. His most blessed followers gain the Two Minds of Madness trait. The creature has advantage on all Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saving throws.",
 "Demonic Boon of Fraz-Urb'luu|MTF": "Fraz-Urb'luu, master of deceit, teaches initiates lies and illusions. They can gain the Liar's Eye trait. The creature has advantage on Wisdom (Insight or Perception) checks. As a bonus action, it automatically detects all illusions and hidden creatures within 15 feet.",
 "Demonic Boon of Goristro|MTF": "A goristro can grant the Labyrinthine Recall trait. The creature can perfectly recall any path it has traveled.",
 "Demonic Boon of Graz'zt|MTF": "Graz'zt teaches cultists to turn pain into pleasure. Cultists gain Joy from Pain. When the creature suffers a critical hit, it can use a reaction to make one melee weapon attack. Cult leaders gain Master of Pleasures. As a reaction to taking damage, the creature magically grants 5 temporary hit points to itself and up to three allies within 30 feet.",
 "Demonic Boon of Juiblex|MTF": "Juiblex's loner followers gain slime toughness. Lesser followers gain Liquid Movement. As an action, the creature moves up to 20 feet through 1-inch spaces, ending where it fits or taking 5 force damage and returning. Devoted followers gain Slimy Organs. It resists nonmagical bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage. On a critical hit against it or at 0 hit points, creatures within 5 feet take acid damage equal to its Hit Dice.",
 "Demonic Boon of Marilith|MTF": "A marilith can grant the Serpentine Reaction trait. The creature gets one extra reaction each round, usable only for an opportunity attack.",
 "Demonic Boon of Nalfeshnee|MTF": "A nalfeshnee can grant the Guarded Mind trait. The creature is immune to the frightened condition.",
 "Demonic Boon of Orcus|MTF": "Orcus sometimes lets followers stay mortal to infiltrate cities. Cultists gain Undying Soul (short or long rest recharge). At 0 hit points, the creature makes a DC 10 Constitution save, and on a success drops to 1 hit point instead. Leaders gain Aura of Death. While not incapacitated, a 30-foot aura, blocked by cover, makes the creature and friendly undead immune to frightened and resistant to radiant damage. Enemies in it have disadvantage on death saves.",
 "Demonic Boon of Yeenoghu|MTF": "Devoted ones gain Gnashing Jaws and Rampage, and leaders gain Aura of Bloodthirst. Gnashing Jaws: melee attack, reach 5 feet, proficiency bonus plus Strength modifier to hit, 1d4 plus Strength modifier piercing. Rampage: after dropping a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, use a bonus action to move half speed and use Gnashing Jaws once. Aura of Bloodthirst: creatures with Rampage within 10 feet can use Gnashing Jaws as a bonus action.",
 "Demonic Boon of Zuggtmoy|MTF": "Zuggtmoy's followers are mostly mindless victims of spores that burrow into the brain and make fanatic servants. Each gains the Spore Kissed trait. The creature is immune to the charmed and frightened conditions. When it drops to 0 hit points, each creature within 10 feet takes poison damage equal to its number of Hit Dice.",
 "Cult of Baphomet|MPMM": "Devotees gain Labyrinthine Recall, perfect memory of paths traveled. Followers gain Unerring Tracker and leaders gain Incite the Hunters. Unerring Tracker: as a bonus action, the creature links psychically to one creature it sees. For 1 hour, it can learn that target's distance and direction as a bonus action. Incite the Hunters (short or long rest recharge): as an action, each ally within 30 feet with Unerring Tracker makes a weapon attack as a reaction against its tracked target.",
 "Cult of Demogorgon|MPMM": "Demogorgon's followers are lone killers driven by his whispering voice. His most blessed followers gain the Two Minds of Chaos trait. The creature has advantage on all Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saving throws.",
 "Cult of Fraz-Urb'luu|MPMM": "Fraz-Urb'luu grants his cultists the Liar's Eye trait. The creature has advantage on Wisdom (Insight or Perception) checks. As a bonus action, it detects all illusions and hidden creatures within 15 feet.",
 "Cult of Geryon|MPMM": "Cult members can gain Crushing Blow (short or long rest recharge). As a bonus action, the creature adds its Strength modifier (minimum +1) to the damage of its next melee weapon hit within 1 minute. Leaders can also gain Indomitable Strength (Recharge 5). As a reaction to taking damage, the creature rolls a d10 and subtracts the result from the damage.",
 "Cult of Graz'zt|MPMM": "Cultists can gain Joy from Pain. When the creature suffers a critical hit, it can use a reaction to make one melee weapon attack. Cult leaders can gain Master of Pleasures. As a reaction to taking damage, the creature magically grants 5 temporary hit points to itself and up to three allies within 30 feet.",
 "Cult of Juiblex|MPMM": "Lesser followers can gain Liquid Movement. As an action, the creature moves up to 20 feet through spaces 1 inch wide, ending where it fits or taking 5 force damage and returning to its start. Devoted followers can gain Slimy Organs. The creature resists nonmagical bludgeoning, piercing and slashing damage. On a critical hit against it or at 0 hit points, it sprays acid, and creatures within 5 feet take acid damage equal to its Hit Dice.",
 "Cult of Orcus|MPMM": "Cultists gain Undying Soul (short or long rest recharge). At 0 hit points, the creature makes a DC 10 Constitution save, and on a success drops to 1 hit point instead. Leaders can gain Aura of Death. While not incapacitated, a 30-foot aura, blocked by cover, makes the creature and friendly Undead immune to frightened and resistant to radiant damage. Enemies in it have disadvantage on death saving throws.",
 "Cult of Yeenoghu|MPMM": "Devoted followers gain Gnashing Jaws and Rampage, and leaders gain Aura of Bloodthirst. Gnashing Jaws: melee attack, reach 5 feet, proficiency bonus plus Strength modifier to hit, 1d4 plus Strength modifier piercing. Rampage: after dropping a creature to 0 hit points with a melee attack on its turn, use a bonus action to move half speed and use Gnashing Jaws once. Aura of Bloodthirst: creatures with Rampage within 10 feet can use Gnashing Jaws as a bonus action.",
 "Cult of Zariel|MPMM": "Loyal cultists can gain Ferocious Surge (short or long rest recharge). When the creature hits with a non-critical attack, it can make the hit a critical hit. Leaders can gain Infernal Tactics. After rolling initiative, if not incapacitated, the creature can swap initiative results among itself and up to three allies it sees.",
 "Cult of Zuggtmoy|MPMM": "Zuggtmoy's cultists are mostly mindless victims of spores that burrow into the brain and make fanatic servants. Each gains the Spore Kissed trait. The creature is immune to the charmed and frightened conditions. At 0 hit points, each creature within 10 feet takes poison damage equal to its number of Hit Dice.",
}
